title: LSP Find References - (Example)

\function lsp.who() [[World]]
\procedure lsp.hello() Hello, <<lsp.who>>!
\widget $lsp.greeting() <strong><<lsp.hello>></strong>

Open this tiddler's `.tid` file in your editor, rest the cursor on any call of `lsp.who` below and press Shift+F12. The list holds every call on this page, the one inside `lsp.hello` at the top of this tiddler, and the definition of `lsp.who` above it. Each call renders ''World'':

* a macro call: <<lsp.who>>
* a `$macrocall` widget: <$macrocall $name="lsp.who"/>
* a `$transclude` widget: <$transclude $variable="lsp.who"/>
* an attribute value: <$text text=<<lsp.who>>/>
* a filter variable: <$list filter="[<lsp.who>]" variable="w"><<w>></$list>
* the `function` operator: <$list filter="[function[lsp.who]]" variable="w"><<w>></$list>
* the function as an operator: <$list filter="[lsp.who[]]" variable="w"><<w>></$list>

A custom widget works the same way. Rest on `$lsp.greeting` in the call below and press Shift+F12 to find it and its `\widget` definition at the top:

<$lsp.greeting/>

Back to [[LSP Find References]].
